$\Theta(\min_{m \in [n]} [(\nicefrac{1}{m} \sum_{i=1}^{m} \nicefrac{1}{h_i})^{-1} \left(\nicefrac{L \Delta}{\varepsilon} + \nicefrac{\sigma^2 L \Delta}{m \varepsilon^2}\right)])$
provided that communication times are negligible. In the worst-case scenario, on the ``very bad function'' \citep{arjevani2022lower}, all these methods perform equally well. Next, we discuss the strengths and weaknesses of the methods that are not captured by the $h_i$-fixed computation model.
